1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:04,231
We used to dare each other to ask Danny's uncle about his arm.

2
00:00:04,281 --> 00:00:06,313
He only ever said one thing.

3
00:00:06,363 --> 00:00:07,398
A wolf took it.

4
00:00:07,448 --> 00:00:09,001
On this street.

5
00:00:09,151 --> 00:00:10,646
We thought he was mad.

6
00:00:10,696 --> 00:00:13,081
Silver nails in the windowsill.

7
00:00:13,131 --> 00:00:15,268
Wolfsbane over the door.

8
00:00:15,318 --> 00:00:17,033
Every full moon,

9
00:00:17,083 --> 00:00:19,313
he sent us home before dark.

10
00:00:19,363 --> 00:00:21,703
Then he'd stand at the end of the road all night.

11
00:00:21,753 --> 00:00:23,613
Watching the houses.

12
00:00:23,763 --> 00:00:26,711
We called him Wolfman Mick.

13
00:00:27,101 --> 00:00:28,684
Mick died last week.

14
00:00:28,734 --> 00:00:30,609
I came home for the funeral.

15
00:00:30,659 --> 00:00:32,431
Slept in my old room.

16
00:00:32,481 --> 00:00:33,031
First full moon in twenty years,

17
00:00:33,081 --> 00:00:37,205
with nobody at the end of the road.

18
00:00:37,674 --> 00:00:39,341
I woke at three.

19
00:00:39,391 --> 00:00:40,621
The window was open.

20
00:00:40,671 --> 00:00:42,250
Mud on the sill.

21
00:00:42,481 --> 00:00:44,231
Then Danny texted.

22
00:00:44,281 --> 00:00:47,115
Mum finally told me how Mick lost his arm.

23
00:00:47,165 --> 00:00:49,186
The summer we were ten.

24
00:00:49,236 --> 00:00:51,296
The night you went missing.

25
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:53,619
I don't remember going missing.

26
00:00:53,769 --> 00:00:56,569
Mick wasn't watching for wolves getting in.

27
00:00:56,679 --> 00:00:59,290
He was watching for one getting out.

28
00:01:01,760 --> 00:01:02,667
Mick?
